I was just wondering, what is the difference between #invoking and #applying
something? Obviously, they do different things :)


There is a rambling story here with a point at the end. Read it (y/n)?

You feal bored.

The #apply command always reminds me of text adventures which had the USE
command. You often didn't have to know how to use an object, you just said
"use..." Kinda silly really, when computers got more memory, I began to see
"How will you use it?" more often.
The first time I went on a quest was with a Valkerie (sp?). I killed Lord
S-whatever, and found the Orb of Fate (or something like that). Seeing as there
were no up stairs, my first thought was - use the Orb. How? By applying it of
course. When that didn't work, I pulled out my hair until I asked for help, and
some kind person told me to #invoke it instead. I had never heard of an invoke
command (it wasn't in 3.0b7, my previous version, and it isn't listed in the
Mac 3.1.1 menu's, unless I am blind).
Point to story: The #apply command, In my mind, was always like the USE
command. I feal that adding an #invoke command was a bit strange. Now, I must
admit, I haven't read all the in game help or kept up with the versions of NH,
but there seems to be no explanation of the difference between the two.

Can somebody please "clue me up"?


